FINDING_ID: IM_F_R3_003
SEVERITY: 0.77
FLAW_CLASS: 1
ABSTRACTION_INDEX: 0.55
DESCRIPTION: In `_extended_p_pass_remediation`, Module 3 (per-model impact assessment) checks `if all(recent[i] < recent[i - 1] for i in range(1, len(recent)) if recent[i - 1] > 0)`. The generator with a conditional `if recent[i-1] > 0` means that if ANY element in `recent[:-1]` is zero, that comparison is skipped. With `recent = [0, 5, 3]`, the generator yields only the comparison `i=2: 3 < 5 = True` (skipping `i=1` because `recent[0] = 0`). `all()` over a single True returns True, so the model is flagged as "findings declining" even though findings went 0→5→3 (recovering then dipping). **Gemini_IM_F_NEW_GENERATOR_FILTER_BUG covers this exact issue.** Withdrawing.

